WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.162 --> 00:00:03.380
(dramatic music)
(roaring)

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.190
- [Narrator] Probably no
other creatures on the planet

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.720
have struck as much fear
and awe in our hearts

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.270
as the dinosaurs.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.437
(roaring)

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.320
The earliest dinosaurs appeared
about 245 million years ago

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.760
during the Triassic Period.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.850
When most of the Earth's
landmasses were still joined

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.210
together as the super continent Pangaea.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.540
Over millions of years Pangaea split apart

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.880
causing the dinosaurs to become separated

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.823
for the very first time.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.760
This led the reptiles to adapt

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.710
to their specific habitats and diversify.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.963
Giving rise to many new dinosaur species.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.090
According to some estimates,

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.913
more than 1,000 species of
dinosaurs have roamed the Earth.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:00.310
All dinosaurs descended from
reptiles called Archosaurs.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:04.320
From there dinosaurs branched
out into two major groups,

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.740
Saurischia and Ornithischia

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.170
based on the shape and
orientation of their pelvis.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.870
In Saurischian dinosaurs,

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:15.120
such as Tyrannosaurus
Rex and Brachiosaurus,

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.120
the pelvis' pubis bone
faces forward and down.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.170
In Ornithischian dinosaurs,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.750
such as Stegosaurus and Hadrosaurs,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.883
the pubis bone faces backward and down.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.310
Across both groups, dinosaurs
varied greatly in size.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.800
Some were small, like Compsognathus,

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.230
which was barely larger than a chicken.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:42.560
Where as others were
gigantic, like Dreadnoughtus,

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.010
which was 85 feet long
and weighed 65 tons,

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:50.473
making it the largest land
animal to have ever lived.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.660
Dinosaur diets varied as well.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:58.040
Herbivores, like Hadrosaurs,

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.040
evolved to have specialized teeth

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.253
for grinding tough plant material.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.580
Carnivores made up roughly
40% of dinosaur species.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.700
Some predators, like
the raptor Deinonychus,

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.543
even hunted in packs.

00:02:14.478 --> 00:02:15.800
(roaring)

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.650
Social behaviors were also
found in other dinosaurs.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.740
Footprints and track ways indicate

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:25.093
that some of the ancient
reptiles traveled together.

00:02:25.093 --> 00:02:29.210
Evidence also shows that herds
may have made annual visits

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.563
to certain sites to lay their eggs.

00:02:33.892 --> 00:02:38.892
But by around 66 million years
ago, most dinosaurs died out.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.063
And the reason why is still a mystery.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.563
The most well known explanation
is an asteroid strike.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.060
But a multitude of factors

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.860
may have contributed to this extinction.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.130
In fact, the dinosaur population

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.200
was already in severe decline

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.323
by the time the asteroid struck.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:04.770
However, several dinosaur
species survived.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:08.073
And some of which evolved
to become today's birds.

00:03:10.484 --> 00:03:14.070
The world has never
again seen land creatures

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.823
as great as the dinosaurs.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.018
But through their descendants
and fossils left behind,

00:03:20.018 --> 00:03:22.233
their legacy lives on.

